cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Coupled Functional Differentiation (CFD): A Mechanism-Based,
  Formalized, and Falsifiable Theory of the Multi-Level Human
  Social System
message: >-
  If you use or reference this theory or any materials in this
  repository, please cite it using the metadata from this file.
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Liran M.
    family-names: Schwartz
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0008-8035-1308'
    city: Haifa
    country: IL
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/LiranOG/Coupled-Functional-Differentiation
url: >-
  https://github.com/LiranOG/Coupled-Functional-Differentiation
abstract: >-
  This repository contains the complete theoretical framework,
  formalization, and empirical propositions for Coupled Functional
  Differentiation (CFD) — a mechanism-based theory of the
  multi-level human social system. The theory specifies a single
  Core Generative Mechanism (CGM) from which macro-level
  coordination, subsystem colonization, small-group logic
  switching, surveillance-capitalism-driven autonomy erosion, and
  globally synchronized crises are derived as deductive
  consequences. Sixteen directional, falsifiable propositions and
  an explicit falsification criterion are provided. This is an
  independent working paper/preprint, not peer-reviewed.
